MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 8de559a088a5d4d48bb00ae8ccc21165, type: 3}
  m_Name: Locust Infestation
  crisisName: Locust Infestation
  ominousWarningText: "At first there are only a few. Farmers notice unfamiliar numbers of insects clinging to grain stalks, gathering along irrigation channels, and rising from the grass whenever workers cross the fields. Most dismiss them as another seasonal nuisance, though older farmers remember stories of years when similar sightings came before devastation. On the horizon, strange dark clouds appear even when the weather is otherwise clear, shifting in ways that ordinary storm clouds do not. Birds gather and scatter unpredictably beneath them. The fields remain green and largely untouched. By evening, however, the horizon itself seems to move."
  obviousWarningText: "The swarm has reached the valley. Thousands of locusts descend ahead of an even larger cloud, filling roads, rooftops, irrigation ditches, and the edges of cultivated fields. Farmers rush to move grain into sealed stores, drive livestock toward shelter, and protect whatever crops can still be covered or harvested early. The sound of wings is now audible long before the insects themselves arrive, a low continuous roar carried across the countryside. Sunlight dims beneath the advancing swarm even though the sky above remains clear. The harvest has not yet been consumed. By morning, entire fields may be covered."
  crisisStartText: "The swarm has descended. Clouds of locusts now move across the countryside, settling onto farms in numbers great enough to strip entire fields bare. Agricultural improvements in affected regions can become infested, reducing their usefulness and placing them at risk of destruction if the insects remain untreated. Workers can clear or repair threatened farmland, while new fields beyond the swarm and strong food reserves can help sustain the population until it passes. The infestation will not remain everywhere forever, but the damage it leaves behind may last far longer than the insects themselves. Every farm saved now is food that will still exist when the skies finally clear."
  ominousWarningTurns: 1
  obviousWarningTurns: 1
  durationTurns: 6
  useAgeWindow: 1
  minimumAge: 4
  maximumAge: 14
